        "subject": "LU-19222 llite: don't force unmount of shared client",
        "message": "LU-19222 llite: don't force unmount of shared client\n\n\"umount -f\" of a bind mount, or of the copy of a Lustre mount in\na container mount namespace, would call ll_umount_begin(), which\nmarks every MDC and OSC import of the client superblock inactive.\nThe kernel calls ->umount_begin() for every MNT_FORCE unmount,\neven when other mounts still use the superblock, so the remaining\nmounts would fail with -ESHUTDOWN until the client was remounted.\n\nThe superblock reference count cannot tell these mounts apart\nfrom the copies held by systemd services in their own mount\nnamespaces, which propagation unmounts with the original mount.\n\nAdd a umount.lustre script, which umount(8) runs for Lustre.  For\n\"-f\", if another mount in this mount namespace has the same client\ninstance (\"lfs getname -i\"), it unmounts without forcing.  Only\nmounts with the same device number are checked, and the check has\na time limit, so it does not block if the servers are unreachable.\n\nIn ll_umount_begin(), do not force an unmount requested from a\nmount namespace other than the one the client was mounted from,\nunless it comes from the initial (host) mount namespace.\nSuch an unmount can still be forced after setting the imports of\nthat filesystem inactive:\n\n    lctl set_param mdc.FSNAME-*.active=0 osc.FSNAME-*.active=0\n\nAdd sanity test_83a for a bind mount and test_83b for a mount\nnamespace.\n\numount(8) runs the helper as a child process and waits for it, so\nconf-sanity test_5a, which kills a running umount, now calls the\nhelper directly, and sanity test_160h counts only the umount\nprocesses in D-state.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity,conf-sanity clientdistro=ubuntu2604 env=SANITY_ONLY=39s+83+247f+413g+421h+900+912,CONF_SANITY_ONLY=4+5a+5d+23a+45\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity,conf-sanity clientdistro=ubuntu2404 env=SANITY_ONLY=39s+83+247f+413g+421h+900+912,CONF_SANITY_ONLY=4+5a+5d+23a+45\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity,conf-sanity clientdistro=sles15sp7 env=SANITY_ONLY=39s+83+247f+413g+421h+900+912,CONF_SANITY_ONLY=4+5a+5d+23a+45\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I54dfd0acacfa1215f36efa38b267547d992540e5\n"
      },
